  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Forecast Verification Bulletin",
    "overview": "A trade plan is treated like a weather forecast. It is issued, stamped with when it was issued and how long it is valid, and later verified against what price did. The interface is the bulletin office: square-cut paper sheets with a heavy printed rule along the top, boxed monospace issue stamps, a masthead with a UTC clock, and faint isobar contours on the chart paper behind everything. It explicitly rejects two looks: the dark neon trading terminal and the soft rounded-card dashboard.\n\nThere are two themes that share every token name. **Day chart** (light) is cool off-white paper with near-black ink. **Radar night** (dark) is deep navy with pale ink. The theme follows the OS preference until the user pins it with the masthead switch (`<html data-theme>`, stored as `alphaboard.theme`); a boot script in `app/layout.tsx` applies the pin before first paint. Any surface that paints its own pixels, such as a chart canvas or an embedded widget, must read the tokens at runtime and rebuild when the theme changes.\n\nDensity is a working desk: compact 12–13.5px UI text, figures in tabular mono, sheets on a 16px gap. Colour is mostly ink on paper. Hue carries meaning: price direction, caution, or emphasis.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Square-cut sheets with a 3px ink top rule over a hairline border",
      "One committed colour field per screen: the isobar-blue band on the trade ticket",
      "Boxed uppercase mono stamps for every issue and validity time, always in UTC",
      "Isobar contour mask behind the whole app, tinted by the `isobar` token",
      "Drawn SVG glyphs (direction triangles, masthead mark, theme icons), never icon fonts or unicode arrows",
      "Every text pair clears WCAG AA (4.5:1) in both themes"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Direction-Only Rule",
        "body": "Green and red mean price direction and nothing else: long/short, target/stop, positive/negative R, candles. Never use them for \"success\" chrome, brand or decoration. Errors borrow `down-soft`/`down` because an error is a stop.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Field Rule",
        "body": "The trade ticket's bulletin band is the one committed colour field on the market screen. Everywhere else the accent is a stroke, a word or a line, never a filled panel.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The AA Both Ways Rule",
        "body": "Every text colour clears 4.5:1 on page, paper, wash and its own `-soft` fill in both themes (the tightest pair, `up` on `page` in day chart, is about 5.0:1). A new token, or a change to an old one, must be re-checked in both themes before it ships.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Figures-Only Mono Rule",
        "body": "Monospace is only for figures and timestamps. Prose, labels and buttons are always Public Sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Eyebrow Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase labels name a field inside a sheet. Never put one above a heading as an eyebrow or kicker; a heading carries its own meaning.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Rule Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from line weight: 3px ink across the top of a sheet, 2px ink under the masthead, 1px hairlines everywhere else. Shadows do not do this job.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the theme tokens (`bg-paper`, `text-ink-2`, `border-line` and so on) for every colour, so both themes work without per-theme code.",
      "Do read tokens with `getComputedStyle` in anything that paints its own pixels, and rebuild it on `useColorScheme()` change.",
      "Do stamp every issued plan with \"Issued\" and \"Valid to\" times in UTC using the boxed mono stamp.",
      "Do set every price, percentage, R multiple and timeframe in mono with tabular figures.",
      "Do draw icons and glyphs as inline SVG coloured with `currentColor` or token classes.",
      "Do give every sheet the square-cut 3px ink top rule.",
      "Do show missing data as missing (\"—\", \"Unavailable\"). Never present an invented number, statistic, testimonial or count.",
      "Do honour reduced motion: animations collapse, the live ping hides, and loading becomes a slow opacity breath."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use `up`/`down` for anything except price direction, or `amber` for anything except caution.",
      "Don't add a second filled accent field to a screen. The ticket band is the only one.",
      "Don't put uppercase eyebrow labels or kickers above headings.",
      "Don't use unicode arrows or icon fonts for direction. Use the drawn DirectionGlyph.",
      "Don't round sheets, or use radii outside the tightened scale.",
      "Don't use mono for prose, labels or buttons.",
      "Don't ship a text colour pair under 4.5:1 in either theme.",
      "Don't drift toward the neon terminal (glow, black-and-green) or the soft card dashboard (large radii, floating shadowed cards)."
    ]
  }
}